{"school":{"dbn":"29Q355","name":"Collaborative Arts Middle School","boro":"Queens","district":"29","district_label":"District 29","report_type":"EMS","report_types":"EMS","school_type":"Middle","grades":"6 to 8","status":"open","enrollment":283,"enrollment_year":"2024-25","address":"145-00 SPRINGFIELD BOULEVARD, QUEENS, NY 11413","phone":"718-977-6180","website":"www.camsq355.org","directory_url":"https://www.myschools.nyc/en/schools/middle-school/71231","accessibility":"Not Accessible","overview":"CAMS is designed to support students through the middle school experience by providing artistically inclined students a space to enhance their creativity. Students major in one studio (dance, instrumental music, or visual arts) for the entirety of their three years at our school. Rejecting punishment as a first step, we guide our students to learn from their experiences using restorative justice approaches as well as positive behavior intervention and support practices. Student empowerment groups, advisory classes, student government, and a school cultural committee keeps us focused on developing the entire child. Understanding that our students are digital natives, we use technology to improve access to learning. Welcoming all learners, our students are diverse in their abilities and backgrounds. Consequently, we are sensitive to planning our instruction to meet students\u00c3\u0083\u00c2\u00a2\u00c3\u0082\u00c2\u0080\u00c3\u0082\u00c2\u0099 differentiated learning needs.  Also, we are broadening our regents offerings so more of our students can earn high school credit while in middle school. As our families are our partners. We enjoy their voices and hands to help do the lifting needed to move our school forward.","start_time":"8:20am","end_time":"2:40pm","languages":null,"subway":null,"bus":"Q111, Q113, Q114, Q3, Q77, Q85","shared_building":"1","neighborhood":"Springfield Gardens","latitude":40.664741,"longitude":-73.759206,"coordinate_source":"geocoded","first_year":